  "description": "What a context publishes or consumes. A `domain-event` is something that happened inside a context, named in the past tense; an `integration-event` crosses a context boundary and is therefore a published contract someone else depends on; a `published-language` is a shared vocabulary for exchange; an `api` is an exposed operation.\n\nWhether the context publishes or consumes decides who owes whom compatibility. A break requires a version bump and a migration, from which a consumed interface is exempt.\n\nAn interface is also the only target a reference crossing a bounded context may name.",
